            {
               "text": "### Images from E Life\n\nThese images are copyright for E Life and allowed to be used according to the license determined by them.\n\nTo visualize all images, use the left and right arrows on the slide below.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p><div class=\"htSlides\"><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">1 / 1</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"imgHNaledi\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgHNaledi', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">The figure includes approximately all the material incorporated in this diagnosis, including the holotype specimen, paratypes and referred material. These comprise 737 partial or complete anatomical elements, many of which consist of multiple reassembled specimens. Specimens not identified to the element level, such as non-diagnostic long bones or cranial fragments, and a subset of fragile specimens are not shown here. The 'skeleton' layout in the center of the photo is a composition of elements representing multiple individuals. This view is in perspective; the table on which the bones are arranged is 120 cm wide for scale reference. © Lee Roger Berger research team  (<htcite0>).</div></div><i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-left htSlidePrev\" onclick=\"htPlusDivs(-1);\"></i><i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-right htSlideNext\" onclick=\"htPlusDivs(1);\"></i></div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>Humans - Who are we? Why are we alone today, when we lived with others in the past? (<htcite1>)</li><li>In this text, we study the development of the empire from an external perspective (<htcite2>).</li><li>Multiplying with the body (Phase 2) - Continuing to multiply with our body, we learn that we are not the only animals to create rituals throughout evolution (<htcite3>).</li></ul></div></div></p>",
               "source": [
